{
  "about": "The continuity ledger (1.2.1): facts the lore tells in more than one file, and the forms each may take. tools/lore/continuity.py --check reads every visible string of the lore (and the hidden facts' text, marked) in each entry's scope and flags a statement that differs. Kinds: value (each claim pattern's group v must be one of allowed; numbers are compared as numbers), forbid (a sentence matching any forbid pattern, and no unless pattern, contradicts the fact), requires (a field matching every pattern in all must also match require). Scope: files (lore ids such as bosses/host), locations (a location's file and the files of its bosses), sentence (a sentence must match it to count), exclude (a sentence matching it is not read) and fields (a regex on the field path, such as ^(?!legend) to leave the fight advice out). Patterns are Python regular expressions, case-insensitive. A \"finding\" says what the check found when this ledger was written and what a fix might be.",
  "facts": [
